# fifo_barrier_root: Barriers on the root FIFO: an index whose slot already holds the value, index 63 with value 0, a value behind the slot by serial arithmetic (0x90000005 against 5), and several barriers at once all run the command. Index 64 and index 0xffffffff fault it. A barrier on the root's own slot for a value beyond the last pushed stamp is a circular wait and faults; 0x103c then names the command's ring offset. 32 barriers on index 0 hit the same check each time.
